From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nix-on-droid <nix-on-droid@local>
Date: Mon, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] execve: reject 32-bit guests with a diagnostic

Companion to strip-32bit-support.patch, which removes the -m32
loader on every architecture.  Without this a 32-bit ELF is still
accepted by open_elf() and then handed the 64-bit loader, so the
guest dies with a bare SIGSEGV and no hint about why.  A few lines
here turn that into an explanation.

The test keys off the ELF class rather than the architecture, so it
covers x86_64 as well: strip-32bit-support.patch removes the loader
there too, and a 32-bit guest would fail just as silently.

It sits after the execve status check on purpose.  The 64-bit loader
can fail for reasons unrelated to the guest's class (ENOMEM,
ETXTBSY, ...), and the guest deserves to see that error rather than a
misdiagnosis about 32-bit support.

---
 src/execve/exit.c |   15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/execve/exit.c b/src/execve/exit.c
index 348a1fd..8b710f3 100644
--- a/src/execve/exit.c
+++ b/src/execve/exit.c
@@ -482,6 +482,21 @@ void translate_execve_exit(Tracee *tracee)
 	if ((int) syscall_result < 0)
 		return;
 
+#if !defined(HAS_LOADER_32BIT)
+	if (IS_CLASS32(tracee->load_info->elf_header)) {
+		/* This build was stripped of 32-bit support (see
+		 * strip-32bit-support.patch), so a 32-bit guest would run
+		 * the 64-bit loader and die with an unexplained SIGSEGV.
+		 * Fail it loudly instead.  Tested after the execve status
+		 * so that a loader which failed for an unrelated reason
+		 * (ENOMEM, ETXTBSY, ...) still reports that reason.  */
+		note(tracee, ERROR, USER, "32-bit ELF executables are not "
+			"supported by this proot build (64-bit only)");
+		terminate_tracee(tracee);
+		return;
+	}
+#endif
+
 	/* The guest program is now running; PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS calls from
 	 * here on belong to the guest, not to PRoot's own pre-execve setup. */
 	tracee->seen_execve = true;
--
2.53.0
